WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.300
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.200
We're hanging out
with Lil Rel Howery.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.000
We'll see him on tour
with Tiffany Haddish.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.167
We're about to play
"Hey, Robot." Here we go.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:14.434
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, robot ♪

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:16.033
♪ Hey, robot ♪

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.267
-Now, here's how it works.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.601
This is based
on the real board game

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:20.100
"Hey, Robot" that
you can play at home.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.467
It's like
the classic game "Password,"

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:24.334
but your partner
is a smart speaker.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:26.000
First, I will pick a card
with a word on it,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.868
and then we'll take turns asking
a question to get the speaker

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:31.434
to say that word
somewhere in the answer.

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:34.367
Okay? If you get it right,
you get a point. Ready for this?

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.667
-Change the name of this game
to "Hey, A.I."

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:39.534
-Yeah, that's basically
what it is.

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:41.534
Okay. Ready for this?

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:54.300
Alexa, name the characters
in "Wizard of Oz."

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.567
-According to fandom,

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:57.501
the main characters
from "The Wizard of Oz"

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:58.934
include Dorothy Gale,

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.334
Professor Marvel,
the carriage driver,

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.467
the Wizard of Oz,
the gatekeeper,

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:05.434
the guard who cries,
the Scarecrow...

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:06.734
[ Ding! ]
Yes. Thank you!

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:10.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:13.868
Carriage driver?
Alexa, stop! Alexa, stop.

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:15.300
No one ever heard
of those other characters.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.734
-What was the order
of that call sheet?

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:18.667
-I don't know.
She said the carriage driver.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.133
I didn't know Dorothy's
last name.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:22.267
What was her name?

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.067
That's a little too specific.

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.467
If you know Dorothy's last name,

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.901
you've seen "Wizard of Oz"
too many times.

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:30.267
Wow! The carriage driver?
Yeah. No one remembers.

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:33.434
Okay, here we go.
Who are you for Halloween?

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:35.767
Hello. I'm the carriage
driver from "Wizard..."

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:37.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.267
-Yeah. That's funny.
-Alright.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:39.300
You're up, bud.
Here you go.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.968
-So, do I not show you what --

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:43.400
-Yeah, you can show me.
I'm playing with you. Right?

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.934
I can show the crowd, too,
if I want to, right?

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:47.234
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:49.601
Uh, you see it.
-Okay.

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:51.200
T-Rex.
-[ Sighs ]

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:56.667
Hey, Siri.
-No.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:58.501
[ Laughter ]
[ Buzzer ]

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:01.200
[ Sad tuba ]

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:04.868
It's Alexa. It's Alexa.
-Oh. Oh.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.200
I'm sorry.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:09.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:15.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.467
Okay.

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.634
I'm sorry. I really am sorry.
Okay, here we go.

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:21.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:25.467
Ah.

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:28.634
Because I wonder if they going
to say that. Ah.

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:30.934
-I think I got it.

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:34.100
-Okay, okay.
Hey, Alexa, um...

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.834
Dinosaurs in "Jurassic Park."

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:40.334
-Sorry, I don't know that.

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:45.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.367
-Wow. I never even
heard her say that before.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:49.534
She doesn't know that there's --

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:53.367
-That's not -- Alexa.

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:59.734
The animal characters
in "Jurassic Park."

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:00.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:03.300
-From fandom.com, pteranodons

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.601
are both enemies and mounts

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:07.901
originating from
the Jurassic Park franchise.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.734
-There you go.
Alright, my turn.

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:11.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:13.667
Oh, wait.
Alright. Ready?

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:16.767
Alexa, who sings
"Get it on, bang a gong"?

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:23.067
Alexa, who sings
"get it on, bang a gong"?

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:26.000
-According to
an Alexa Answers contributor,

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.567
"Bang a Gong, (Get It On)"

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:29.968
was sang
by English rock band T-Rex.

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:32.467
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:37.300
-♪ Get it on ♪

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.734
♪ Bang a gong ♪

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:40.534
♪ Get it on ♪

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:42.501
♪♪

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:44.400
♪ Get it on ♪

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.701
♪ Bang a gong ♪

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:46.968
♪ Get it on ♪

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:50.801
♪♪

00:03:52.868 --> 00:03:55.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.167
-How did you --

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:58.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.100
-I don't know why. I just --

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:04.234
-That's such a random
song choice,

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:06.167
but also to know the -- like,
you know how some songs

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:09.000
you hear, like, you're not
going to know the band?

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.133
Yeah. Alright. T-Rex.

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:11.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:13.200
-Alright. Here, you can go.
You can take this next one.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.300
Come on.
I want you to get this.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.567
-Okay.
Why are you holding on to it?

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:17.501
-Sorry.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:21.601
-Okay. It's -- Okay.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:23.467
You know what I mean?
This has got to be easy.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:24.601
You see this?

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.601
-I think so.

00:04:26.601 --> 00:04:31.000
-Hey, Alexa, name
some cities in Tennessee.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.133
-This might answer
your question.

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:35.767
Nashville, Memphis,
Knoxville, Chattanooga.

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:37.467
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:38.767
-Come on now.

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:41.067
That's how you play the game.

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:48.601
Okay.

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:51.033
Yeah. This should be easy,
right?

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:52.167
-Yeah.

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:56.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:57.934
-Or is it?

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:09.367
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:12.801
Alexa, Hubba Bubba --

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:18.200
Alexa, Hubba Bubba
is a type of what?

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.868
-This might answer
your question.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.200
Bubble gum.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.300
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.601
-Wow!

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:25.968
What?!

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:27.767
Dude! That's all she --

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:30.501
That's crazy.
That's all she said.

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:32.734
Dude, I loved
having you on the show.

00:05:32.734 --> 00:05:35.467
I don't know. We weren't playing
against each other.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:38.834
We were playing with each other.
That's my man, Lil Rel Howery.

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:40.934
He's on tour
with Tiffany Haddish.

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:42.300
Go check out some of these dates

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.267
right here on the
Best Friends Comedy Tour.

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:46.934
Lil Rel Howery, everybody.

00:05:46.934 --> 00:05:49.033
Congratulations
on your engagement, buddy.

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:50.400
You're the best.
We'll be right back, everybody.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.968
Stick around. Come on back.

